        "body": "I'm experiencing critical iOS build and runtime issues with Calf v0.8.0 when using it in a Kotlin Multiplatform project. The issue manifests differently depending on the version combination:\n\n1. **With Compose Multiplatform 1.8.2**: iOS build fails with IR lowering compilation error\n2. **With Compose Multiplatform 1.9.0-rc02**: Build succeeds but app crashes at runtime when opening screens with Calf DatePicker\n\n  ## Environment\n\n- **Calf version**: 0.8.0\n- **Kotlin version**: 2.2.0\n- **KSP version**: 2.2.0-2.0.2\n- **Target platforms**: Android, iOS, Desktop\n- **iOS SDK**: 18.0\n- **Xcode**: 16.0\n\n## Reproduction Steps\n\n### Scenario 1: Build Failure (Compose Multiplatform 1.8.2)\n\nUsing these versions in `gradle/libs.versions.toml`:\n```\n  [versions]\n  kotlin = \"2.2.0\"\n  composeMultiplatform = \"1.8.2\"\n  navigationCompose = \"2.9.0-beta02\"\n  calfUi = \"0.8.0\"\n\n  Result: iOS build fails with:\n  Compilation failed: IR lowering failed at: CurrencySelectionBottomSheet.kt\n  java.lang.Exception: IR lowering failed at: CurrencySelectionBottomSheet.kt\n  Compilation finished with errors\n```\n\n### Scenario 2: Runtime Crash (Compose Multiplatform 1.9.0-rc02)\n\nUsing these versions:\n```\n  [versions]\n  kotlin = \"2.2.0\"\n  composeMultiplatform = \"1.9.0-rc02\"\n  navigationCompose = \"2.9.0-beta03\"\n  calfUi = \"0.8.0\"\n```\n\nResult:\n- iOS build succeeds ✅\n- App crashes when navigating to any screen containing Calf DatePicker component ❌\n\nCode Sample\n```\nThe failing component uses Calf DatePicker in a bottom sheet:\n  // CurrencySelectionBottomSheet.kt\n  @Composable\n  fun CurrencySelectionBottomSheet(\n      // ... parameters\n  ) {\n      // Bottom sheet containing Calf UI components\n      AdaptiveDatePicker(\n          // ... configuration\n      )\n  }\n\n  Build Configuration\n\n  // build.gradle.kts (composeApp module)\n  kotlin {\n      listOf(\n          iosX64(),\n          iosArm64(),\n          iosSimulatorArm64()\n      ).forEach { iosTarget ->\n          iosTarget.binaries.framework {\n              baseName = \"ComposeApp\"\n              isStatic = true\n              export(\"com.mohamedrejeb.calf:calf-ui:0.8.0\") // Properly exported as per docs\n          }\n      }\n\n      sourceSets {\n          commonMain.dependencies {\n              api(\"com.mohamedrejeb.calf:calf-ui:0.8.0\")\n          }\n      }\n  }\n```\n\n  Expected Behavior\n\n  The app should:\n  1. Build successfully for iOS with Kotlin 2.2.0 and recent Compose Multiplatform versions\n  2. Run without crashes when using Calf DatePicker components\n\n  Actual Behavior\n\n  - With Compose MP 1.8.2: Compilation fails with IR lowering error\n  - With Compose MP 1.9.0-rc02: Runtime crash on DatePicker usage\n\n  Additional Context\n\n  - The issue only affects iOS; Android and Desktop targets work fine\n  - All other non-Calf components work correctly\n  - The framework is properly exported as per documentation\n\n  Workaround Attempts\n\n  1. ✅ Exporting calf-ui to iOS framework (already done)\n  2. ❌ Trying different Compose Multiplatform versions (1.8.2 vs 1.9.0-rc02)\n  3. ❌ Clean builds and pod cache clearing\n\n  Questions\n\n  1. Is Calf 0.8.0 compatible with Kotlin 2.2.0?\n  2. Are there any known issues with Compose Multiplatform 1.9.0-rc02?\n\n  This is blocking our iOS release. Any guidance would be greatly appreciated!\n",
